00:20:11.030 --> 00:20:14.130
Christy and I had our
own plan that the kids

00:20:14.130 --> 00:20:17.880
didn't know about that we
needed to put into action

00:20:17.880 --> 00:20:18.713
that night.

00:20:19.891 --> 00:20:22.500
I'm pretty sure this is Christy's idea

00:20:22.500 --> 00:20:24.770
but I was, the moment she said it,

00:20:24.770 --> 00:20:26.850
we were out on a date, we're like,

00:20:26.850 --> 00:20:28.420
we gotta, we were talking about,

00:20:28.420 --> 00:20:29.743
we got to figure out what we're gonna do,

00:20:29.743 --> 00:20:33.820
this is our first Christmas
here in LA with the kids

00:20:33.820 --> 00:20:36.020
as opposed to going back home.

00:20:36.020 --> 00:20:38.560
We got to start developing
some traditions, you know,

00:20:38.560 --> 00:20:40.670
like I've been talking about,

00:20:40.670 --> 00:20:42.930
and then she pitched this idea

00:20:42.930 --> 00:20:46.650
and I immediately knew, as
she started to pitch it,

00:20:46.650 --> 00:20:49.210
just jump onboard, don't even analyze it,

00:20:49.210 --> 00:20:51.322
you now how I have a tendency to like

00:20:51.322 --> 00:20:52.337
tweak and analyze.

00:20:52.337 --> 00:20:54.610
- Oh, really, you have
a tendency to analyze?

00:20:54.610 --> 00:20:56.160
- Yeah but I can do this
and it will be better

00:20:56.160 --> 00:20:59.700
or what if we did, I was
like, I was just, yes man.

00:20:59.700 --> 00:21:02.200
It was a brilliant idea.

00:21:02.200 --> 00:21:03.969
- You should use that more often.

00:21:03.969 --> 00:21:04.802
(Rhett and Link laugh)

00:21:04.802 --> 00:21:05.635
- Just with her.

00:21:07.400 --> 00:21:08.793
The idea was,

00:21:09.800 --> 00:21:12.473
Christmas morning, scavenger hunt.

00:21:14.140 --> 00:21:15.513
Kids are gonna come down,

00:21:16.980 --> 00:21:18.750
well, we don't have an upstairs,

00:21:18.750 --> 00:21:21.180
we do, but it's just me
and Christy's upstairs,

00:21:21.180 --> 00:21:24.539
all the house is downstairs
for everybody else, you know,

00:21:24.539 --> 00:21:26.570
you gotta use the pecking order here,

00:21:26.570 --> 00:21:28.322
so they're all downstairs.

00:21:28.322 --> 00:21:30.779
They're gonna flow out into

00:21:30.779 --> 00:21:33.680
and go to the Christmas tree where

00:21:33.680 --> 00:21:35.050
all the presents are

00:21:36.190 --> 00:21:38.190
and then they're gonna find out,

00:21:38.190 --> 00:21:42.621
oh, uh-uh, ain't no
presents under the tree.

00:21:42.621 --> 00:21:46.228
The tree was like full
of presents under there,

00:21:46.228 --> 00:21:49.370
so we moved all of them and

00:21:50.350 --> 00:21:53.800
hid them all around the
house, outside of the house,

00:21:53.800 --> 00:21:58.710
in the washing machine,
in the grill, in the car

00:21:58.710 --> 00:22:03.710
and then we had one bear,
unwrapped, with a card on it

00:22:04.697 --> 00:22:07.070
and it had the first clue

00:22:07.070 --> 00:22:09.360
and boy, we were so excited about it.

00:22:09.360 --> 00:22:10.193
(Rhett laughs)

00:22:10.193 --> 00:22:12.202
You know and then you'd
open that up and it was

00:22:12.202 --> 00:22:15.260
a letter and it was--

00:22:15.260 --> 00:22:16.630
- From the bear?

00:22:16.630 --> 00:22:17.830
- No.

00:22:17.830 --> 00:22:19.233
A letter from us and it was,

00:22:21.268 --> 00:22:23.980
it even rhymed, it was
a poem that I wrote.

00:22:23.980 --> 00:22:27.220
Yeah, man and at the end
it had the first clue

00:22:27.220 --> 00:22:28.250
