00:41:16.200 --> 00:41:18.890
So, it was a very different
feeling that kind of

00:41:18.890 --> 00:41:22.560
stuck up on me, that's
like, we have a thing

00:41:23.430 --> 00:41:26.330
and I think that it was something that

00:41:26.330 --> 00:41:30.670
my family, that encouraged
us to do our own thing,

00:41:30.670 --> 00:41:33.025
I think they knew better than I did

00:41:33.025 --> 00:41:35.920
that's it like, yes, you
need to have this sensation

00:41:35.920 --> 00:41:38.770
and I realize that I just had not had it

00:41:38.770 --> 00:41:42.030
and when I realized that I was having it,

00:41:42.030 --> 00:41:46.180
I started to cry and it
was very, I was very happy.

00:41:46.180 --> 00:41:47.950
- Does this mean that you're gonna,

00:41:47.950 --> 00:41:49.363
like this Christmas now?

00:41:50.620 --> 00:41:51.530
You're not gonna be home anymore?

00:41:51.530 --> 00:41:53.810
- I don't, yeah, I don't know.

00:41:53.810 --> 00:41:56.470
- I mean, as long as Locke
keeps playing basketball,

00:41:56.470 --> 00:41:57.820
we have to be here.

00:41:57.820 --> 00:42:01.087
So, I don't have a choice
for four years but--

00:42:02.122 --> 00:42:04.100
- I mean, at this point,

00:42:04.100 --> 00:42:05.610
we haven't talked about that specifically,

00:42:05.610 --> 00:42:07.441
so I don't know exactly.

00:42:07.441 --> 00:42:08.910
- But it sounds like it was pretty moving.

00:42:08.910 --> 00:42:10.360
- It was very moving, so yeah,

00:42:10.360 --> 00:42:13.200
that is a big tick in the yes column

00:42:13.200 --> 00:42:15.850
of let's do this again, let's
continue to build on this.

00:42:15.850 --> 00:42:19.050
- Well, I will say, I teared up

00:42:20.350 --> 00:42:22.450
at the Christmas meal but it was because

00:42:23.410 --> 00:42:25.300
I nearly burned the house down

00:42:25.300 --> 00:42:27.180
and it was just the smoke
coming from the oven.

00:42:27.180 --> 00:42:28.140
- What?

00:42:28.140 --> 00:42:28.973
- Yeah,

00:42:29.990 --> 00:42:31.040
but it was beef.

00:42:31.040 --> 00:42:34.049
- I'm sure this was my
wife's fault, so go for it.

00:42:34.049 --> 00:42:35.510
- But it wasn't beef stroganoff,
it was Beef Wellington.

00:42:35.510 --> 00:42:37.230
- Ah, that's not easy.

00:42:37.230 --> 00:42:38.103
- Well so,

00:42:39.300 --> 00:42:42.500
Jessie's parents had
been in town, they left,

00:42:42.500 --> 00:42:45.040
we had a couple days, we kind of did some

00:42:45.040 --> 00:42:48.720
just the us McLaughlin's thing and then

00:42:51.060 --> 00:42:53.720
Jessie's sister and her family,

00:42:53.720 --> 00:42:55.720
so husband and two boys,

00:42:55.720 --> 00:42:57.940
about, you know, high school age boys,

00:42:57.940 --> 00:42:59.573
so a little older than Locke,

00:43:00.700 --> 00:43:03.720
were gonna come stay but
they flew in on Christmas Day

00:43:04.750 --> 00:43:07.020
and so we're like, okay,
well, we're gonna prepare

00:43:07.020 --> 00:43:09.120
Christmas dinner so we
can all have it together

00:43:09.120 --> 00:43:11.900
when the get there and Jessie and I,

00:43:11.900 --> 00:43:16.900
we fancy ourselves as culinarily skilled,

00:43:16.930 --> 00:43:19.610
although we're not but
we're adventurous and

00:43:21.010 --> 00:43:23.100
we were like, she's like,
well, I'm gonna do these

00:43:23.100 --> 00:43:26.260
Cornish hens because we
do Cornish hens every year

00:43:26.260 --> 00:43:29.280
as our Christmas dinner
before we go back home

00:43:29.280 --> 00:43:31.454
but now we're gonna make
it at Christmas dinner

00:43:31.454 --> 00:43:33.630
but I was like, but what if
we tried Beef Wellington?

00:43:33.630 --> 00:43:36.490
Ever since I watched that
first season of Hell's Kitchen

00:43:36.490 --> 00:43:38.100
and heard Gordon Ramsey talk about it,

00:43:38.100 --> 00:43:40.750
I had this idea of how awesome it would be

00:43:40.750 --> 00:43:43.880
to make Beef Wellington,
so we made all of them

00:43:43.880 --> 00:43:44.773
at the same time.

00:43:46.422 --> 00:43:47.723
- That's ambitious.

00:43:49.021 --> 00:43:54.021
- (sighs) We ended up, we couldn't put

00:43:54.120 --> 00:43:55.920
all of it in the oven at the same time

00:43:55.920 --> 00:43:59.130
and we ended up putting the
hens directly on the grate

00:43:59.130 --> 00:44:01.750
in the oven and then put
these drip pans underneath it

00:44:01.750 --> 00:44:03.920
and then everything was
dripping off of the Cornish hens

00:44:03.920 --> 00:44:05.770
and it was smoking up the
house and the fire alarm

00:44:05.770 --> 00:44:08.700
kept going off and it was
freezing, as you know,

00:44:08.700 --> 00:44:11.010
for LA, it was freezing on Christmas Day,

00:44:11.010 --> 00:44:14.500
it was in the 40s, can you believe it,

00:44:14.500 --> 00:44:16.330
which is super cold to us at this point,

00:44:16.330 --> 00:44:18.900
'cause, you know, we've adjusted,

00:44:18.900 --> 00:44:21.920
so I got all of the
windows and doors open.

00:44:21.920 --> 00:44:23.790
I did tear up a little bit, but again,

00:44:23.790 --> 00:44:26.150
it was because of the smoke in the eyes.

00:44:26.150 --> 00:44:28.053
- There were no flames though, just smoke?

00:44:28.053 --> 00:44:28.886
- No, no flames and actually--

00:44:28.886 --> 00:44:29.719
- Was there yelling?

00:44:29.719 --> 00:44:33.540
- The meal, Jessie and
I, yeah, a little bit.

00:44:33.540 --> 00:44:34.450
- Christmas Day yelling?

00:44:34.450 --> 00:44:35.713
- I mean, it's not--

00:44:35.713 --> 00:44:36.716
- hey, that's part of it, man.

00:44:36.716 --> 00:44:37.570
- It's not Christmas if you're
not yelling at each other.

00:44:37.570 --> 00:44:39.010
- Yeah.

00:44:39.010 --> 00:44:39.843
It's part of it.

00:44:39.843 --> 00:44:41.540
- And the meal was really good.

00:44:41.540 --> 00:44:43.420
It ended up being great,
nothing was burned.

00:44:43.420 --> 00:44:47.020
It was just the drippings had
created the smoke situation.

00:44:47.020 --> 00:44:47.853
- Okay.

00:44:49.520 --> 00:44:50.630
- I don't know if I'm gonna make that,

00:44:50.630 --> 00:44:52.720
the smoking up the house, a tradition

00:44:52.720 --> 00:44:54.440
but it is the kind of thing that

00:44:54.440 --> 00:44:55.370
