00:52:30.200 --> 00:52:31.100
- It's pretty big.

00:52:33.550 --> 00:52:35.890
For one, there's a rock called Bell Rock,

00:52:35.890 --> 00:52:39.543
which is pretty freaking big but you can,

00:52:40.440 --> 00:52:42.900
if you're physically
capable, you could hike up

00:52:42.900 --> 00:52:45.380
to the top of the Bell in an hour, okay,

00:52:45.380 --> 00:52:47.060
so that gives you an idea how big it is.

00:52:47.060 --> 00:52:49.280
It's shaped kind of like a bell.

00:52:49.280 --> 00:52:50.200
We hiked this.

00:52:50.200 --> 00:52:51.823
It is a vortex.

00:52:52.890 --> 00:52:54.703
The entire formation.

00:52:55.890 --> 00:52:56.850
- Is a vortex.

00:52:56.850 --> 00:52:58.010
- Is a vortex.

00:52:58.010 --> 00:52:58.843
- Okay.

00:52:58.843 --> 00:53:00.420
- That's all I can say about it.

00:53:00.420 --> 00:53:02.140
- You didn't feel it?

00:53:02.140 --> 00:53:03.000
Did you feel it?

00:53:03.000 --> 00:53:05.290
- I felt joy being there.

00:53:05.290 --> 00:53:09.810
I felt exhilaration and
a little fear climbing up

00:53:09.810 --> 00:53:11.367
because Lando kept wanting to climb up

00:53:11.367 --> 00:53:12.910
and I kept saying,

00:53:12.910 --> 00:53:15.310
climbing up's easy buddy,
it's the climbing down

00:53:15.310 --> 00:53:16.910
that's difficult.

00:53:16.910 --> 00:53:18.920
- But in a vortex you don't
have to worry about gravity.

00:53:18.920 --> 00:53:20.370
- That's what he said.

00:53:20.370 --> 00:53:21.203
- Oh.

00:53:21.203 --> 00:53:23.880
- And I was like, nope, I'm not buying it,

00:53:23.880 --> 00:53:25.637
so every so often I would make him

00:53:25.637 --> 00:53:29.370
crawl ahead and then prove to me that

00:53:29.370 --> 00:53:31.910
he could crawl back down
and the rest of the family

00:53:31.910 --> 00:53:34.560
had long since bailed on this entire.

00:53:34.560 --> 00:53:35.960
- They didn't go up into the vortex?

00:53:35.960 --> 00:53:38.010
- We went, they went halfway up the Bell

00:53:38.010 --> 00:53:40.710
and then we went another
third of the way up,

00:53:40.710 --> 00:53:42.550
beautiful place, just can't,

00:53:42.550 --> 00:53:44.700
I have nothing more to say about a vortex.

00:53:44.700 --> 00:53:47.170
I don't know, I just
didn't experience anything,

00:53:47.170 --> 00:53:48.260
I should have signed up for the tour.

00:53:48.260 --> 00:53:49.093
- You weren't open.

00:53:49.093 --> 00:53:50.150
- I should have got--

00:53:50.150 --> 00:53:51.632
- You were closed.

00:53:51.632 --> 00:53:52.465
- We should have got the woman in our car.

00:53:52.465 --> 00:53:54.033
- You have to open your
heart in the same way

00:53:54.033 --> 00:53:57.160
that the vortex is open and
then you'd understand it.

00:53:57.160 --> 00:54:00.500
- We did have a couple
of magical experiences.

00:54:00.500 --> 00:54:01.990
The first one, we get there that night,

00:54:01.990 --> 00:54:04.230
we're eating pizza and then
the employees at the place say,

00:54:04.230 --> 00:54:07.100
oh look, it's, there's a snow flurry,

00:54:07.100 --> 00:54:08.670
it's the first of the season.

00:54:08.670 --> 00:54:10.680
- Was it going in a vortex pattern.

00:54:10.680 --> 00:54:11.960
- It was not.

00:54:11.960 --> 00:54:13.030
- That would have been important for me.

00:54:13.030 --> 00:54:15.810
- They went outside and it was like wow,

00:54:15.810 --> 00:54:18.400
they actually don't get
a lot of snow there,

00:54:18.400 --> 00:54:19.470
'cause I was reading online and it's like

00:54:19.470 --> 00:54:21.780
if you're hiking, you might
be lucky and there might be

00:54:21.780 --> 00:54:24.660
a dusting of snow on the red
rocks, which can be beautiful.

00:54:24.660 --> 00:54:27.510
Turns out, Lando had never
seen, I didn't realize this,

00:54:27.510 --> 00:54:30.203
he had never seen falling,
natural falling snow.

00:54:31.190 --> 00:54:32.023
- Hmm.

00:54:32.023 --> 00:54:32.856
- You know?

00:54:32.856 --> 00:54:33.770
'Cause we'd been out here since he was,

00:54:33.770 --> 00:54:36.104
before he was two years old and

00:54:36.104 --> 00:54:40.050
he hasn't seen snowfall except for manmade

00:54:40.050 --> 00:54:43.230
at a ski resort last year at this time.

00:54:43.230 --> 00:54:45.200
That was special but then the next day I

00:54:45.200 --> 00:54:50.183
take him out hiking or on
a nature walk, wink, wink,

00:54:51.050 --> 00:54:54.660
and it starts snowing and
we went on a hike, dude,

00:54:54.660 --> 00:54:58.870
in the snow and it was awesome.

00:54:58.870 --> 00:54:59.703
I mean, it was like--

00:54:59.703 --> 00:55:01.610
- This is where I saw
some of the Instagram's

00:55:01.610 --> 00:55:02.879
from your family, right?

00:55:02.879 --> 00:55:05.217
- Yeah, it's like nothing,
I mean, it's like,

00:55:05.217 --> 00:55:07.630
you can go your whole
life and not hike in snow

00:55:07.630 --> 00:55:10.580
falling on the red rocks,
especially in Sedona,

00:55:10.580 --> 00:55:11.630
from what I've heard.

00:55:12.741 --> 00:55:14.950
It was pretty special.

00:55:14.950 --> 00:55:15.962
We had a blast.

00:55:15.962 --> 00:55:16.820
- Did you cry then?

00:55:16.820 --> 00:55:19.422
- I had a little tear action happening.

00:55:19.422 --> 00:55:20.300
- And there was no beef
stroganoff involved?

00:55:20.300 --> 00:55:21.489
- No, not at all.

00:55:21.489 --> 00:55:24.257
- 'Cause you need to
isolate what the trigger is.

00:55:24.257 --> 00:55:25.090
- Yeah, trying to correlate what it is.

00:55:25.090 --> 00:55:25.923
- If it's not beef stroganoff,

00:55:25.923 --> 00:55:27.530
it may be just being with your family

00:55:27.530 --> 00:55:29.360
and having good times.

00:55:29.360 --> 00:55:30.572
- Well, how sad is that?

00:55:30.572 --> 00:55:31.405
(Rhett laughs)

00:55:31.405 --> 00:55:32.883
It's gotta be something else.

00:55:36.200 --> 00:55:39.210
The next day, we took a
Jeep tour which turned out

00:55:39.210 --> 00:55:41.950
to be actually kind of lame
but you can rent Jeeps there

00:55:41.950 --> 00:55:42.783
and do--

00:55:43.820 --> 00:55:45.153
- Extreme off-roading?

00:55:45.153 --> 00:55:45.986
- Aggressive off-roading,

00:55:45.986 --> 00:55:47.870
which, in a lot of
places you can't do that,

00:55:47.870 --> 00:55:49.190
so that's another cool thing about that

00:55:49.190 --> 00:55:51.240
if you wanna go to Sedona, not a sponsor.

00:55:52.249 --> 00:55:53.434
- Sedona, not a sponsor.

00:55:53.434 --> 00:55:54.455
(Rhett and Link laugh)

00:55:54.455 --> 00:55:56.290
An entire town, not a sponsor.

00:55:56.290 --> 00:55:58.420
- The next to last day we're there,

00:55:58.420 --> 00:55:59.950
it starts snowing.

00:55:59.950 --> 00:56:04.311
We go out for brunch and
this is an unexpected snow

00:56:04.311 --> 00:56:06.720
and it's dumping snow.

00:56:06.720 --> 00:56:09.120
By the time we come out
an hour and a half later,

00:56:09.120 --> 00:56:12.233
we had driven four minutes to eat brunch.

00:56:13.200 --> 00:56:15.210
We come out, we get back in the car,

00:56:15.210 --> 00:56:17.690
it's like seven inches of snow.

00:56:17.690 --> 00:56:19.260
It's crazy.

00:56:19.260 --> 00:56:21.270
It was amazing.

00:56:21.270 --> 00:56:23.710
It took us over two hours to drive

00:56:23.710 --> 00:56:28.710
the four minute drive
back to our condo because

00:56:28.950 --> 00:56:30.350
the place just wasn't ready for it.

00:56:30.350 --> 00:56:31.390
It shut down.

00:56:31.390 --> 00:56:33.370
We drove for an hour,
we didn't move hardly

00:56:33.370 --> 00:56:36.220
and I was like, alright guys,
get out and just walk home

00:56:36.220 --> 00:56:38.760
and they had a blast
just kind of walking home

00:56:38.760 --> 00:56:41.733
in the snow blast and
I had some alone time

00:56:41.733 --> 00:56:43.913
with my vortex.

00:56:45.240 --> 00:56:46.073
That sounded weird.

00:56:46.073 --> 00:56:48.159
I was just in the car listening to--

00:56:48.159 --> 00:56:48.992
- Yeah, understood.

00:56:48.992 --> 00:56:50.710
- But I listened to like--

00:56:50.710 --> 00:56:51.543
- Vortex music.

00:56:51.543 --> 00:56:53.740
- Spa music, it was really--

00:56:53.740 --> 00:56:55.550
- You got get everything in line.

00:56:55.550 --> 00:56:56.910
- It was really,

00:56:56.910 --> 00:56:59.500
and then, so we get back home,

00:56:59.500 --> 00:57:01.367
have some coffee, I finally get there

00:57:01.367 --> 00:57:03.010
and the sun's going down and I'm like,

00:57:03.010 --> 00:57:05.730
we can hike back up this
trail from our condo

00:57:05.730 --> 00:57:08.210
and Lando and I went out
there and that's the picture

00:57:08.210 --> 00:57:12.080
that I showed in LTAT that
I got him to take of me

00:57:12.080 --> 00:57:13.720
and I get up there to the top

00:57:13.720 --> 00:57:17.780
and dude, I swear, this
is when I cried again.

00:57:17.780 --> 00:57:21.850
I was like, Lando, this
is the most beautiful

00:57:21.850 --> 00:57:22.900
thing I've ever seen.

00:57:24.265 --> 00:57:26.020
There's was snow on this trail and you

00:57:26.020 --> 00:57:29.220
have view of the red
rocks and it was as quiet

00:57:30.680 --> 00:57:34.150
as Christmas Eve before Santa and

00:57:35.020 --> 00:57:36.590
I called Christy, I was like,

00:57:36.590 --> 00:57:38.410
you bail on this but
you have to get dressed

00:57:38.410 --> 00:57:40.950
and you have to hike up here and see this

00:57:40.950 --> 00:57:42.320
and she came up there and
she was like tearing up,

00:57:42.320 --> 00:57:44.590
it was so beautiful up there and so quiet

00:57:44.590 --> 00:57:46.857
and she was like, this is like Narnia

00:57:46.857 --> 00:57:49.600
and I thought about you and
your obsession with Narnia.

00:57:49.600 --> 00:57:51.440
Dude, I went to Narnia.

00:57:51.440 --> 00:57:52.273
- Did you find a lamp post?

00:57:52.273 --> 00:57:53.950
- I went to winter Narnia, no lamp post.

00:57:53.950 --> 00:57:54.870
- It wasn't Narnia.

00:57:54.870 --> 00:57:56.170
- Took lots of photos.

00:57:56.170 --> 00:57:59.923
- Did you find any goat tracks?

00:58:01.220 --> 00:58:02.053
- No.

00:58:03.861 --> 00:58:05.890
Okay, it wasn't actually Narnia, I get it.

00:58:05.890 --> 00:58:08.340
- But just one set, just a set of two

00:58:10.658 --> 00:58:12.203
'cause he was half goat.

00:58:13.920 --> 00:58:18.920
- I mean, the entire thing, I was just,

00:58:19.010 --> 00:58:23.090
I was just struck with, for my family,

00:58:23.090 --> 00:58:26.410
I try to adopt this mentality but then I'm

00:58:26.410 --> 00:58:28.180
trying to apply it to life
and a New Year's resolution

00:58:28.180 --> 00:58:30.290
type way is just trying to,

00:58:30.290 --> 00:58:31.270
maybe we've talked about this,

00:58:31.270 --> 00:58:35.500
but to set up, you can't
create moments like that

00:58:35.500 --> 00:58:37.050
or all the moments that we had,

00:58:38.305 --> 00:58:41.900
the tear-up moments, but
you can set the table

00:58:41.900 --> 00:58:44.270
for something memorable to happen,

00:58:44.270 --> 00:58:47.150
for the place to get filled
up with smoke, so to speak,

00:58:47.150 --> 00:58:48.750
you know and it's just,

00:58:48.750 --> 00:58:50.550
there's an art to saying, okay,

00:58:50.550 --> 00:58:52.920
I can't force this but I can set the table

00:58:52.920 --> 00:58:54.120
for something amazing.

00:58:54.120 --> 00:58:55.060
We can go here.

00:58:55.060 --> 00:58:57.270
We can go to this place and do a walk and

00:58:57.270 --> 00:58:59.150
maybe the snow will dump,

00:58:59.150 --> 00:59:01.130
maybe something magical will happen.

00:59:01.130 --> 00:59:03.250
- It might have been a
totally different trip

00:59:03.250 --> 00:59:05.154
if it hadn't snowed.

00:59:05.154 --> 00:59:08.277
- You know, I can't say it's
not related to the vortex.

00:59:08.277 --> 00:59:10.533
- But the vortex isn't at your house.

00:59:11.479 --> 00:59:12.480
- Why not?

00:59:12.480 --> 00:59:13.700
- Maybe you have a vortex at your house?

00:59:13.700 --> 00:59:14.533
- Maybe I do.

00:59:14.533 --> 00:59:15.840
- Maybe vortexes make you cry.

00:59:15.840 --> 00:59:16.940
- Maybe they do.

00:59:16.940 --> 00:59:21.030
- I had a slightly different,
slightly different experience.

00:59:21.030 --> 00:59:22.513
- No snow in Mexico.

00:59:23.789 --> 00:59:24.810
Caba-licious.

00:59:24.810 --> 00:59:29.810
- I enjoyed being with the
family that we had in town

00:59:30.160 --> 00:59:32.280
but I have a certain capacity for just

00:59:32.280 --> 00:59:34.830
people at my house and
regardless of how well

00:59:34.830 --> 00:59:37.243
we're getting along and
the fun that we're having.

00:59:37.243 --> 00:59:38.076
- I get it.

00:59:38.076 --> 00:59:40.890
- We had a great time, as families,

00:59:40.890 --> 00:59:43.030
we watched a lot of movies.

00:59:43.030 --> 00:59:46.163
I saw Bird Box, suddenly
all the memes made sense.

00:59:47.047 --> 00:59:51.188
Saw Aqua Man, I watched
my wife watch Jason Momoa.

00:59:51.188 --> 00:59:52.021
- Oh.

00:59:52.021 --> 00:59:53.719
- And that was interesting
but I got to take in

00:59:53.719 --> 00:59:56.290
Amber Heard in sort of a similar way,

00:59:56.290 --> 00:59:59.023
which I had license to do that.

00:59:59.023 --> 01:00:00.060
- Oh.

01:00:00.060 --> 01:00:02.410
- In her Aqua suit or whatever it was.

01:00:02.410 --> 01:00:03.573
- I heard that.

01:00:04.630 --> 01:00:05.463
- And then,

01:00:07.510 --> 01:00:10.450
so we saw movies but by the end of it

01:00:10.450 --> 01:00:12.650
I was kind of like, I am,

01:00:12.650 --> 01:00:15.320
I kind of and I knew this and this is why

01:00:15.320 --> 01:00:16.790
I planned this trip to
Cabo with just Jessie,

01:00:16.790 --> 01:00:19.720
I was like, I'm gonna
need some time to myself

01:00:19.720 --> 01:00:20.920
and just me and my wife

01:00:21.800 --> 01:00:23.670
after having everybody in town.

01:00:23.670 --> 01:00:27.340
So we went down to Cabo,
just for like four days

01:00:28.690 --> 01:00:31.403
and had a very relaxing time.

01:00:31.403 --> 01:00:33.869
I actually ended up working

01:00:33.869 --> 01:00:35.713
but I don't call it work 'cause, you know,

01:00:35.713 --> 01:00:38.100
like writing songs and
working on some other things

01:00:38.100 --> 01:00:40.250
we can't talk about,

01:00:40.250 --> 01:00:43.250
but stuff that you could do next to a pool

01:00:43.250 --> 01:00:45.030
in sort of a relaxing fashion

01:00:46.970 --> 01:00:50.720
and I got the, and did the photo shoot,

01:00:50.720 --> 01:00:54.260
which, you know, I'm
very proud of (laughs).

01:00:54.260 --> 01:00:56.170
- Well, you gotta fill the listeners in

01:00:56.170 --> 01:00:58.350
'cause they don't know
what the photo shoot is,

01:00:58.350 --> 01:00:59.992
I don't think you said that at the top.

01:00:59.992 --> 01:01:02.350
- Well, no, yeah so,

01:01:02.350 --> 01:01:03.770
when we got to this place,

01:01:03.770 --> 01:01:07.970
they were orienting us
to what was, you know,

01:01:07.970 --> 01:01:10.340
the options and the
place and they were like,

01:01:10.340 --> 01:01:12.370
oh, there's a complimentary photo shoot.

01:01:12.370 --> 01:01:14.950
I knew that by complimentary
photo shoot they meant,

01:01:14.950 --> 01:01:16.630
somebody's gonna take
photos of you and then

01:01:16.630 --> 01:01:18.180
charge you a lot of money for the photos

01:01:18.180 --> 01:01:19.620
that they took, it's not
really complimentary.

01:01:19.620 --> 01:01:23.140
- So the shoot is free but
the photos are expensive?

01:01:23.140 --> 01:01:27.370
- But Jessie had gotten me
this watermelon bathing suit

01:01:27.370 --> 01:01:31.810
and matching watermelon
shirt, almost as a joke,

01:01:31.810 --> 01:01:33.570
not ever thinking I
would wear them together.

01:01:33.570 --> 01:01:35.500
I've worn them both independently.

01:01:35.500 --> 01:01:36.650
I think I wore the watermelon shirt

01:01:36.650 --> 01:01:37.900
on the show at one point.

01:01:38.930 --> 01:01:40.780
But I put the whole package together,

01:01:41.690 --> 01:01:44.170
if there's any place
to do it, it's Cabo and

01:01:45.020 --> 01:01:46.710
I was like, this is what I'm
wearing for the photo shoot,

01:01:46.710 --> 01:01:47.840
what are you wearing?

01:01:47.840 --> 01:01:49.900
So, Jessie and I took some photos together

01:01:49.900 --> 01:01:52.250
but then I was like, obviously I gotta get

01:01:52.250 --> 01:01:53.310
something by myself.

01:01:53.310 --> 01:01:55.810
I mean, this is kind of a special outfit.

01:01:55.810 --> 01:01:58.393
- Okay, now tell me why that was obvious?

01:02:00.320 --> 01:02:02.290
- Just because, I mean.

01:02:02.290 --> 01:02:03.200
(Rhett laughs)

01:02:03.200 --> 01:02:04.624
You saw the photo.

01:02:04.624 --> 01:02:06.630
(Rhett laughs)

01:02:06.630 --> 01:02:08.594
I think I created a vortex in Cabo.

01:02:08.594 --> 01:02:09.913
- Oh, gosh.

01:02:09.913 --> 01:02:10.746
Give me a break.

01:02:10.746 --> 01:02:12.106
- I don't know how the vortexes happen but

01:02:12.106 --> 01:02:13.260
if there was not a vortex
around me while I had

01:02:13.260 --> 01:02:15.250
that watermelon suit on on the beach,

01:02:15.250 --> 01:02:16.680
then I don't believe in vortexes.

01:02:16.680 --> 01:02:18.310
- Oh, gosh.

01:02:18.310 --> 01:02:20.970
- And the interesting thing was is

01:02:20.970 --> 01:02:23.990
you know me, of the two of us,

01:02:23.990 --> 01:02:28.990
I'm the one that is a little more worried

01:02:29.040 --> 01:02:30.000
about what people think.

01:02:30.000 --> 01:02:31.141
- Uh-huh.

01:02:31.141 --> 01:02:36.141
- And also, I'm always, I'm
very overly irrationally

01:02:37.580 --> 01:02:39.700
sensitive to how big I am.

01:02:39.700 --> 01:02:41.380
I'm just a very large person,

01:02:41.380 --> 01:02:43.140
so I kind of feel like,

01:02:43.140 --> 01:02:46.180
if I do anything, if I
get out there and dance,

01:02:46.180 --> 01:02:48.130
whatever I do, you're gonna see me do it

01:02:48.130 --> 01:02:49.930
because you can't miss me, right?

01:02:49.930 --> 01:02:50.763
- [Link] Right.

01:02:50.763 --> 01:02:51.916
- And so--

01:02:51.916 --> 01:02:52.900
- And you're not even factoring in

01:02:52.900 --> 01:02:54.680
being covered in watermelons.

01:02:54.680 --> 01:02:55.513
- You're right and so,

01:02:55.513 --> 01:02:57.497
I'm like, I gotta put this watermelon on,

01:02:57.497 --> 01:02:58.900
I'm gonna walk all around this resort.

01:02:58.900 --> 01:03:00.250
- You're getting cold feet on us.

01:03:00.250 --> 01:03:01.250
- No, I knew I was gonna do it

01:03:01.250 --> 01:03:03.860
but I couldn't just relax into it.

01:03:03.860 --> 01:03:05.970
I wanted to just relax into my identity

01:03:07.079 --> 01:03:09.150
as the guy who wears
the watermelon outfit.

01:03:09.150 --> 01:03:10.950
